# SCOPE 4  |  Tier 2 saddle points: B3LYP-D3(BJ)/def2-TZVP, OptTS + FREQ
# State: W-TS steam hydrolysis saddle  |  register row: W-TS-T2-V05
# Start: TIER 1 candidate optts2_bandD_ci (1 imaginary mode, -226.10 cm-1; barrier
#      +29.29 kJ/mol vs W-PRC, still pending A4).
# Why: the steam baseline is the one pathway with a published benchmark range
#      (76-125 kJ/mol, Silaghi et al. 2015). A Tier 2 barrier inside that range is a
#      strong validation statement for the whole model.
# Pre-registered rule: same A4 test as V-TS2; if it fails, say so.
# Cost warning: OptTS with an exact initial Hessian (%geom Calc_Hess true) on 30
#      atoms is the most expensive job class in this package; treat 10-60 h per job
#      as the honest bracket and run them one at a time with a budget stop.
# Gate: TERMINATED NORMALLY + converged + exactly 1 imaginary mode animating the
#      reacting bond; then the A4 displacement test.

! B3LYP D3BJ def2-TZVP RIJCOSX def2/J TightSCF DefGrid3 OptTS Freq

%pal nprocs 4 end
%maxcore 3000

%scf
  MaxIter 300
end

%geom
  Calc_Hess true
  MaxIter 200
end

%freq
  Temp 298.15, 1003.15
end

* xyzfile 0 1 xyz/w-ts.xyz
